WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.784
The incident check reads incidents
created in the last thirty days, and every

2
00:00:04.784 --> 00:00:07.299
incident still active, with their alerts,

3
00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:09.888
using Learn's list call
with expand alerts.

4
00:00:09.888 --> 00:00:11.287
Each one gets a finding.

5
00:00:11.287 --> 00:00:13.800
Triaged: open, with an owner.

6
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.138
Untriaged: open, no owner,
but inside its window.

7
00:00:18.138 --> 00:00:22.850
Overdue triage: no owner,
past its window, which fails.

8
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.712
Closed: resolved with a
classification and a determination.

9
00:00:26.712 --> 00:00:30.037
And closed without
classification, which also fails.

10
00:00:30.037 --> 00:00:34.345
The windows come from the guide's
severity table: one hour for high,

11
00:00:34.345 --> 00:00:38.413
twenty-four for medium, seventy-two
for low and informational.

12
00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:43.440
Containment stays on the response ladder;
the kit only prints each incident's rung.
